  "question": {
    "text": "Assume that the radius of the first Bohr orbit of hydrogen atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8491;</mo></math>. The radius of the third Bohr orbit of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is _____ picometer. (Nearest Integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "270",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For hydrogen like species, from Bohr&#39;s formulas we get,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mfrac></math><br />where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;is orbit number,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>&nbsp;is atomic number</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>Thus,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#8491;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>270</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>270</mn><mi>pm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}